reply.body:
I've been playing around with this code some and see that `indexRequest.getPipeline()` and `getFinalPipeline()` are never actually null, so this code already works. But, I think it would be more obvious that there isn't a chance of an NPE if we flip the equality check to `NOOP_PIPELINE_NAME.equals(indexRequest.getPipeline())` as you described; which will work well. 

Alternatively, we could move this logic into `PipelineIterator`, and make use of the `NOOP...` check that it already does. Eg, we could add something like this to `PipelineIterator`
```
 public Pipeline peekFirst() {
            return getPipeline(defaultPipeline != null ? defaultPipeline : finalPipeline);
 }
```
then set `firstPipeline` a few lines down after creating `PipelineIterator`. 

I am fine with this, or the existing method if you think it doesn't belong in `PipelineIterator`

